---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Countdown from '../../components/Countdown.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Are there difficulty settings? How punishing is death?",
    a: "Scavland uses named game modes rather than Easy/Normal/Hard sliders. The official announcements list Explorer, Returner and Iron Man. Explorer was added in the Day One Patch (Update 0.5.169) for players who want a less punishing experience: you keep your equipment when you die (not all backpack items), Jobs reward Money and Reputation faster, combat is more forgiving, and autosave is enabled. Beyond what the mode descriptions on the death screen say, the announcements do not document the exact penalties for Returner and Iron Man, so we do not claim any."
  },
  {
    q: "What is the state of base building and progression?",
    a: "The announcements describe a Safehouse-centred loop rather than free-form building. Update 0.5.169 added a second Player Stash at the hospital and increased stash capacity, with all stash locations sharing one inventory. Update 0.7.0 added crafting tables and stashes to all main camps, made stash expansions purchasable from a Trader for 50,000 Rubles, rebuilt the Death Screen, and gave each run its own autosave slot. No modular exterior base building, and no Act II or Act III structure, is documented in the announcements we hold."
  },
  {
    q: "Is there a macOS or console release? How does it run on Steam Deck?",
    a: "Scavland launched on Steam as a PC release: the store page lists Windows only, so we cannot confirm any native macOS build or console version. For handheld play, the developers state the game was designed with Steam Deck and handheld play in mind and the store page lists Full controller support; Update 0.7.0 also notes improved text sizing on Steam Deck. No Valve Deck compatibility badge is listed on the store page."
  },
  {
    q: "Is melee combat viable against mutants and armored patrols?",
    a: "The announcements we hold do not include a developer statement on melee viability, so we do not claim one. What the store page and patch notes do describe is a hardcore survival RPG built around 25+ firearms and hundreds of weapon parts, where maintenance and repair matter: weapons can explode below 30% condition since Update 0.5.169, and Update 0.7.0 made repairs significantly less punishing and increased weapon durability across the arsenal."
  },
  {
    q: "How does Scavland compare to Zero Sievert?",
    a: "Both sit in the top-down post-apocalyptic extraction genre, but we do not hold a head-to-head comparison source, so this page sticks to Scavland's own documented features. The launch announcement states the game grew from a small project to around 15 developers, with a world roughly 3x larger, procedurally generated underground bunkers, 25+ weapons and hundreds of weapon parts and attachments, 10 factions with unique identities, and a faction and trader reputation system."
  }
];

const roadmap = [
  {
    phase: "Early Access launch",
    timeline: "4 September 2026",
    status: "Shipped",
    items: [
      "Scavland entered Steam Early Access; the announcement is titled \"SCAVLAND IS OUT NOW!\".",
      "Store page features: Single-player, Steam Achievements, Full controller support, DualSense/DualShock support, Steam Cloud and Family Sharing.",
      "The developers describe a world roughly 3x larger, procedurally generated underground bunkers, 25+ weapons and hundreds of weapon parts and attachments, 10 factions and a rebuilt UI."
    ]
  },
  {
    phase: "Day One Patch — Update 0.5.169",
    timeline: "5 September 2026",
    status: "Shipped",
    items: [
      "Added the Explorer game mode: keep your equipment on death (not all backpack items), faster Job rewards, autosave.",
      "Lit campfires now heal you while your Energy and Hydration are good.",
      "A second Player Stash was added at the hospital, stash capacity was significantly increased, and all stash locations share one inventory.",
      "New medical blueprints: Advanced Bandage, Army AI-2, IFAK and Stimpack — sold by Alexei.",
      "AI no longer shoots from outside the screen; player stamina was doubled; Gun Field Tools no longer require Gun Lube."
    ]
  },
  {
    phase: "Update 0.6.0",
    timeline: "9 September 2026",
    status: "Shipped",
    items: [
      "Sleeping in beds to skip time; the world keeps running while you sleep and taking damage wakes you.",
      "The Controls & Keybinding system was completely rebuilt, with rebindable actions, hold/tap variants and an Action Hint Bar.",
      "Jobs overhaul: multiple tracked Jobs, partial Fetch turn-ins and a Reputation cost for cancelling.",
      "Trader specialisation, an armour durability rebalance, weapon range increases and an early version of Simplified Chinese localisation."
    ]
  },
  {
    phase: "Update 0.7.0 (plus Hotfixes 0.7.1 & 0.7.2)",
    timeline: "16 September 2026",
    status: "Shipped",
    items: [
      "Stash expansions purchasable from a Trader for 50,000 Rubles; crafting tables and stashes added to all main camps.",
      "Death Screen rebuilt with proper actions, with full gamepad support.",
      "A major durability and repair pass: weapons last significantly longer, jamming is less frequent, and much of the arsenal was buffed.",
      "Hotfix 0.7.2 rebalanced Raisa diplomat jobs and resolved world chunk loading issues.",
      "Improved text sizing on Steam Deck."
    ]
  },
  {
    phase: "What comes next",
    timeline: "No date published",
    status: "Not dated",
    items: [
      "The developers state that \"the final stretch is all about testing, polishing, balancing, and listening to feedback as we prepare to open the gates to Zalesye\".",
      "No dated feature roadmap, and no release date for a full version, appears in the announcements we hold — so this page does not invent phases, features or dates."
    ]
  }
];
---

<Layout 
  title="Scavland Release Date & Early Access Guide — Scavland Wiki" 
  description="Official Scavland Steam Early Access launch hub: Day 1 playable content, $19 pricing, difficulty rules, community FAQ, and the 2026-2027 development roadmap." 
  keywords="Scavland release date, Scavland Early Access, Steam launch, Scavland price, Scavland roadmap, Scavland difficulty, Scavland base building" 
  canonical="/release-date/"
>
  <Fragment slot="schema">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      '@context': 'https://schema.org',
      '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
      itemListElement: [
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Scavland Wiki', item: 'https://scavland.wiki/' },
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Early Access & Roadmap', item: 'https://scavland.wiki/release-date/' }
      ]
    })} />
  </Fragment>

  <article class="article-shell">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="font-size:0.82rem;color:var(--text-muted,#888);margin-bottom:1.25rem;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:0.4rem;align-items:center;">
      <a href="/" style="color:var(--acid,#b9e86c);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Scavland Wiki</a>
      <span style="opacity:0.4;">/</span>
      <span style="color:#bbb;">Early Access &amp; Roadmap</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="article-header">
      <div style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:4px 10px;background:rgba(185,232,108,0.1);border:1px solid var(--acid,#b9e86c);border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:12px;">
        <span style="display:inline-block;width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--acid,#b9e86c);"></span>
        <span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:0.75rem;color:var(--acid,#b9e86c);font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.05em;">Early Access Launched September 4, 2026</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="page-title">Scavland Early Access Launch &amp; Official Roadmap</h1>
      <p class="lede">Complete overview of Scavland’s Day 1 Early Access content scope, pricing policy, community decision FAQ, and the multi-phase development roadmap.</p>
      <span class="evidence">Evidence: Steam Official Announcement + Community Lead Developer Q&amp;A</span>
    </header>

    <div class="article-layout">
      <div class="article-content">
        <!-- Live Status Component -->
        <Countdown />

        <!-- Key Launch Facts Box -->
        <div class="quick-answer" style="margin-bottom:32px;">
          <strong style="color:var(--acid);font-size:1.05rem;">Confirmed Launch Key Facts</strong>
          <ul style="margin:8px 0 0;padding-left:18px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--ink);">
            <li><strong>Official EA Release:</strong> September 4, 2026 (Global Release)</li>
            <li><strong>Pricing Policy:</strong> $19.00 USD (10% launch week discount at $17.10). Developer NoShadow has committed to maintaining this low entry price throughout Early Access.</li>
            <li><strong>Platform:</strong> PC via Steam (Apple Silicon macOS version under Apple store review).</li>
            <li><strong>Community Traction:</strong> Launched with more than 230,000 Steam wishlists worldwide.</li>
            <li><strong>Launch Scale:</strong> Complete Act I territory, 25+ firearms, 300+ attachment modifications, 10 interacting factions, and the dynamic Mist hazard.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 1: Day 1 Scope -->
        <h2 id="content">What Is Included in the Day 1 Early Access Build?</h2>
        <p>Scavland enters Steam Early Access not as a barebones prototype, but as a fully realized Act I survival sandbox with dozens of hours of replayable progression:</p>

        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));gap:16px;margin:20px 0;">
          <div style="padding:16px;background:#121a16;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;">
            <div style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;color:var(--acid);font-size:0.8rem;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:4px;">Overworld &amp; Bunkers</div>
            <h4 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#fff;">The Zalesye Exclusion Zone</h4>
            <p style="margin:0;font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.5;">Handcrafted open-world sectors including toxic wetlands, industrial rail yards, decayed villages, and procedurally seeded subterranean Soviet bunkers.</p>
          </div>

          <div style="padding:16px;background:#121a16;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;">
            <div style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;color:var(--acid);font-size:0.8rem;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:4px;">Tactical Arsenal</div>
            <h4 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#fff;">25+ Weapons &amp; 300+ Attachments</h4>
            <p style="margin:0;font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.5;">Deep ballistic gunplay featuring 6 ammo calibers, modular optics, suppressors, foregrips, drum magazines, and realistic fouling/jam mechanics.</p>
          </div>

          <div style="padding:16px;background:#121a16;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;">
            <div style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;color:var(--acid);font-size:0.8rem;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:4px;">Living Faction Ecosystem</div>
            <h4 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#fff;">10 Dynamic Factions</h4>
            <p style="margin:0;font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.5;">The store page lists a faction and trader reputation system: earn standing and unlock tiered trade options as you progress.</p>
          </div>

          <div style="padding:16px;background:#121a16;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;">
            <div style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;color:var(--acid);font-size:0.8rem;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:4px;">Environmental Hazard</div>
            <h4 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#fff;">The Mist</h4>
            <p style="margin:0;font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.5;">The store page names "the deadly Mist" as one of the hazards you survive alongside mutants, hostile survivors and radiation.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="article-media">
          <img src="/images/screenshots/steam_ss_08.webp" alt="Official Scavland sector map and launch zones" />
          <p class="caption">The overworld of Zalesye features handcrafted overworld sectors coupled with procedural bunker seeds</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 2: Community Decision FAQ -->
        <h2 id="faq">Top Community Questions &amp; Purchasing Decisions</h2>
        <p>Before stepping into Zalesye, here are authoritative answers to the most common questions raised by players on Steam Discussions and YouTube:</p>

        <div class="faq-list" style="margin:20px 0 35px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px;">
          {faqs.map((faq) => (
            <div style="padding:16px 20px;background:#121a16;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;">
              <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;font-size:1.1rem;color:#fff;display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:8px;">
                <span style="color:var(--acid);font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:0.9rem;">Q:</span>
                {faq.q}
              </h3>
              <p style="margin:0;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.6;color:var(--ink);padding-left:22px;">
                {faq.a}
              </p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <!-- Section 3: Development Roadmap -->
        <h2 id="roadmap">Official Development Roadmap (2026 – 2027)</h2>
        <p>Developer NoShadow has committed to a transparent, multi-stage roadmap as Scavland matures toward full commercial 1.0 release:</p>

        <div class="roadmap-timeline" style="margin:24px 0 35px;position:relative;border-left:2px solid var(--line);padding-left:24px;margin-left:8px;">
          {roadmap.map((stage) => (
            <div style="position:relative;margin-bottom:32px;">
              <!-- Marker Dot -->
              <div style={`position:absolute;left:-31px;top:4px;width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:50%;${
                stage.status === 'Active In Progress' ? 'background:var(--acid);box-shadow:0 0 10px var(--acid);' : 'background:var(--muted);'
              }`}></div>

              <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
                <span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--acid);">{stage.timeline}</span>
                <span style={`font-size:0.7rem;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:3px;${
                  stage.status === 'Active In Progress' ? 'background:rgba(185,232,108,0.15);color:var(--acid);border:1px solid rgba(185,232,108,0.3);' :
                  'background:rgba(255,255,255,0.05);color:var(--muted);'
                }`}>
                  {stage.status}
                </span>
              </div>

              <h3 style="margin:0 0 10px;font-size:1.25rem;color:#fff;">{stage.phase}</h3>
              <ul style="margin:0;padding-left:18px;color:var(--ink);font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.7;">
                {stage.items.map((item) => (
                  <li>{item}</li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <h2 id="next">Explore the Scavland Field Guides</h2>
        <div class="related-grid">
          <a href="/weapons/"><strong>Weapons &amp; Attachments Database</strong><br/>Detailed stats on all 25+ guns, ammo penetration, and 300+ attachment slots</a>
          <a href="/system-requirements/"><strong>System Requirements</strong><br/>PC hardware specifications &amp; Steam Deck testing</a>
          <a href="/factions/"><strong>10 Factions &amp; Outposts</strong><br/>Reputation ranks, trade hubs, and faction-exclusive contracts</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
        <strong>On this page</strong>
        <a href="#content">Day 1 Content Scope</a>
        <a href="#faq">Community Decision FAQ</a>
        <a href="#roadmap">Official Roadmap</a>
        <a href="#next">Field Guides</a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
